AutoName: GeoJoystick
Summary: Mock-location joystick for Android development and testing
Description: |-
  GeoJoystick is an open-source Android mock-location joystick for emulator and developer testing.

  It uses Android's standard mock-location provider flow and manual Developer Options selection. A floating overlay lets users move a selected mock location without repeatedly switching back to the main app. GeoJoystick does not try to hide or bypass Android mock-location status.

  Locations can be chosen with manual coordinates, the OpenStreetMap-based picker, supported map-link import, or optional explicit-submit place/address search. The map supports panning and two-finger pinch-to-zoom, and invalid or failed external input leaves the current selection unchanged.

  GeoJoystick includes compact and expanded joystick layouts, speed presets and custom speed, favorites, restore-last-position, overlay controls, System/Light/Dark appearance, and 17 UI languages.

  Network use is optional and tied to explicit features. The app has no ads, accounts, analytics, tracking, subscriptions, billing, or proprietary updater.

